From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: blurbery <271863866+blurbery@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ad_spdif: derive the E-AC-3 carrier rate from the stream

Each E-AC-3 frame of 1536 samples travels in an IEC 61937 burst of 6144
carrier frames, so the carrier must run at four times the stream's own
sample rate. Upstream fixes it at 192000 Hz, which only fits streams coded
at 48 kHz; for a 44.1 kHz stream mpv's audio timestamps then run about 9%
fast.

Build the E-AC-3 muxer and output format at four times the codec rate
probed for the stream, or at 4 x 48000 when the probe found none. AC-3 is
unchanged (its carrier is the codec rate, 48000 when unknown), the channel
count stays 2 and nothing new is logged. The AVFoundation audio output
divides by four again to time passthrough, so both sides must agree.

Applies to mpv v0.41.0 with upstream commit 1388a453 (patch 0001), whose
cached codec rate it uses.

